    "title": "How to watch Suns-Trail Blazers play-in game - Arizona Sports",
    "text": "The Phoenix Suns’ NBA Play-In Tournament game against the Portland Trail Blazers on Tuesday will be streamed exclusively on Prime Video. Fans can catch the game live on the Arizona Sports app, 98.7 and ArizonaSports.com. The action tips off at 7 p.m. MST following the conclusion of the Miami Heat-Charlotte Hornets play-in game. Here Come the Suns gets underway at 6 p.m., followed by pre-game coverage at 6:30 p.m. on 98.7 and YouTube. On the call for the games will be play-by-play voices Ian Eagle, Kevin Harlan and Michael Grady. They’ll be joined by analysts Brent Barry, Jim Jackson and Stan Van Gundy. Time: 7 p.m. MST Location: Mortgage Matchup Center (Phoenix) TV: Prime Video Radio: Arizona Sports app, 98.7 Suns enter Play-In Tournament vs. Trail Blazers This marks the first time Phoenix has qualified for the play-in. The Suns are 3.5-point favorites, according to FanDuel Sportsbook. Phoenix could be at full strength for the tilt, with guard Grayson Allen the only Suns player on the injury report. He’s listed as questionable with left hamstring soreness. The winner of Suns-Trail Blazers will advance to the NBA playoffs as the No. 7 in the Western Conference and face the No. 2 seed San Antonio Spurs in a seven-game series. A seven-game series against the No. 2 seed San Antonio Spurs awaits the winner. The loser will go on to face the winner of the Golden State Warriors-Los Angeles Clippers matchup. The winner from that game claims the No. 8 seed in the Western Conference, while the loser is eliminated from playoff contention. Whoever comes out of that game will then take on the No. 1 seed Oklahoma City Thunder.",
